Native widescreen, forward paths: no added polygon with a corner the GTE cannot place.

Measured with tuning/wide_view_sweep (every camera path, every 4th node and
the last, the game's own camera at rest, 16:9): on forward paths 0052's camera
test added polygons that reach into the extra columns but cross the eye
plane - 416,153 of 1,280,809 additions, a third. The world renderer has no
near test (0x80042420 RTPT straight into the screen test and the
ordering-table slot), and behind the eye the GTE's saturated division lands a
corner near twice its camera offset from the centre, inside the screen: such
a polygon was drawn as a wedge, in places over the whole frame (S0000015,
S000001A) or as a slab across the top (S0000020). The game's own lists avoid
these; side-on paths have refused them since 0053.

crash2_wide_slst.h: c2sl_fwd_keep() - on forward paths a candidate is kept
when c2wg_classify calls it C2WG_WIDE and every corner is c2wg_placeable; a
pool candidate by the side-on pool's rule (none reach forward paths yet). The
header comment states the rule for every path.

Across the game's forward views (14,495; the sweep, before / after):
- 4:3 pixels changed by the hook 0.419% -> 0.369%, its wedges there 0.102%
  -> 0.053% (the game's own lists draw 0.053%);
- wedge pixels in the extra columns 0.24% -> 0.16% (the rest are the game's
  own polygons reaching there);
- gaps unchanged (3.97%): the refused polygons drew nothing useful.

tuning/wide_frustum_sim checks it: frustum_ref.fwd_keep, an exported forward
case per level with a wedge refused (176 cases), sim.c holding every forward
addition to the rule - C equals the reference on every case, 3,916 wedges
refused.

